## Common flows

These chains show how skills compose. The first is the **repo's own dev
workflow** (how changes to this repo are made); the rest are firmware/NAS task
flows.

### Repo dev workflow (this repo)
```
setup-matt-pocock-skills (once per repo: issue-tracker, triage labels, domain docs)

# plan & track work (mattpocock) — issue-tracking lane; build wiring DEFERRED
to-prd     (conversation → PRD, published to issue tracker, tagged ready-for-agent)
to-issues  (plan / spec / PRD → grabbable issues, tracer-bullet slices, self-tagged)
triage     (manage unlabeled / needs-eval issues — not a required step)
improve-codebase-architecture (find refactor candidates → human feeds to-prd/to-issues)

# build a ready-for-agent issue (superpowers + flow-dev)
ready-for-agent issue
  → converge (by ambiguity shape: intent-unclear → superpowers:brainstorming;
              bug/root-cause → superpowers:systematic-debugging;
              already fully-specified → skip straight to spec)
  → superpowers:writing-plans → docs/superpowers/specs/
  → flow-dev (spec gate → stacked PRs → red-replay + code-review → integration → merge)
        ↳ each Dev task runs superpowers:test-driven-development (red → green)

# verify (superpowers): verification-before-completion
# note: the converge-by-shape + deferred mattpocock build-lane follow the
#       intent-dev-build-test design (docs/prd/…-intent-dev-build-test-orchestrator-design.md)
```

### End-to-end feature development
```
flow-dev → (optional) ubiquiti-flow → ubiquiti-pr-ci-watch → code-review → merge
```

### NAS performance investigation
```
ubiquiti-device-reserve → ubiquiti-deploy-storage → ubiquiti-deploy-nas-fs
  → ubiquiti-nas-perf-test → ubiquiti-test-results
```

### Release cut
```
semver-release fix|minor|major
  → release-note
  → release-announce github-release,github-wiki[,confluence]
```

### Support bundle root-cause
```
ubiquiti-support-debug → ubiquiti-gw-network | ubiquiti-nogw-network
```

